Labels for background objects are drawn in front of discs. Each object's label should carry the same Z-index as the object itself.

The End key is a loophole around time dilation. Holding down + gets the viewer closer and closer to the speed of light, while never reaching it due to relativity. But if the viewer presses End, their speed increases past c in to warp speed and bypasses the relativistic effects. End should apply the same relativistic calculations as +; the only way to go to warp should be pressing W.
